  "description": "K₃NaMnCl₆ crystallizes in the trigonal R̅3c space group. K is bonded in a 8-coordinate geometry to eight equivalent Cl atoms. There are a spread of K-Cl bond distances ranging from 3.23-3.37 Å. Na is bonded in a 6-coordinate geometry to six equivalent Cl atoms. All Na-Cl bond lengths are 2.86 Å. Mn is bonded in an octahedral geometry to six equivalent Cl atoms. All Mn-Cl bond lengths are 2.56 Å. Cl is bonded to four equivalent K, one Na, and one Mn atom to form a mixture of distorted corner, edge, and face-sharing ClK₄NaMn octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles range from 0-64°.",
